id: psalm-a-day
title: A psalm a day
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: The 150 psalms in order, one a reading, with the longest, Psalm
  119, read in 11 parts of 16 verses: 160 readings in all.
suits: Readers who want a short reading each day, most of them a minute or
  two, on its own or beside another plan.
schedule: sequence
behaviors: pace, finish-date
reading-days: 7
coverage: books
canon: protestant
books: PSA
limitations: It reads the Psalms only. Psalms differ greatly in length,
  from Psalm 117's two verses to Psalm 78's seventy-two, so the longest
  readings take five or six minutes. The psalms are numbered as in most English
  Bibles, which follow the Hebrew numbering; Bibles that follow the Greek
  and Latin numbering, as some Catholic and Orthodox Bibles do, number most
  of the psalms from 10 to 147 one lower (Psalm 23 is their Psalm 22).
instructions: Read the next reading whenever you read, in any Bible. If you
  miss a day, your next reading waits for you. At one reading a day, the
  plan takes about five months.
source: An original plan by Day by Word: the psalms in order, one a
  reading. Psalm 119 is written in 22 stanzas of 8 verses, one for each
  letter of the Hebrew alphabet; the plan reads two stanzas at a time, so
  that each part is about as long as a typical psalm. Reading times are
  estimated from word counts of the World English Bible, a public-domain
  translation; the plan can be read in any translation.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
